# NVSHMEM Graph Traversal

Distributed Graph500-style BFS and SSSP using CUDA, MPI, and NVSHMEM.

Library code is in `src/`; the runnable example is `examples/graph500_runner.cu`.

## Requirements

- Linux with an NVIDIA GPU and compatible CUDA driver/toolkit.
- CUDA compiler (`nvcc`).
- MPI implementation with development headers, such as OpenMPI.
- NVSHMEM built with CUDA and MPI support.
- GNU Make.

The Makefile defaults to `/usr/local/cuda`, `/opt/nvshmem`, and the system OpenMPI path. Override `CUDA_HOME`, `NVSHMEM_HOME`, or `MPI_HOME` when needed.

## Build

```sh
make
```

## Run

```sh
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 NVSHMEM_BOOTSTRAP=mpi \
mpirun --allow-run-as-root -np 1 ./build/graph500_runner 12 16
```

Arguments are `SCALE` and optional `edgefactor` (default: `16`).

Set `SKIP_BFS=1`, `SKIP_SSSP=1`, `SKIP_VALIDATION=1`, or `WRITE_DOT=1` as needed.

## GPU Assignment

MPI rank `r` uses GPU `r % gpu_count`. Ranks sharing a GPU share its compute resources; the default NVSHMEM arena size divides available GPU memory among those ranks. Set `NVSHMEM_SYMMETRIC_SIZE` to override that memory size.
